.TITLE "whoami"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the current username. It reports the __effective user ID__ of the user currently logged into the terminal session.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**whoami**
Displays the username associated with the current terminal session.
> 

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __whoami__ is a quick way to verify which account you are using, especially after switching users with __su__ or __sudo__. It is functionally equivalent to running __id -u -n__.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:who** **mac:id**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/whoami.html__
